# Agent instruction hygiene

Path-scoped routing only. Canonical ownership:

- Constitution: root `AGENTS.md` (+ path-scoped `AGENTS.md`)
- Cursor adapters: `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`
- Procedures: `.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md`
- Registry/evals: `planning/skills/skills-registry.yaml`, `tools/skills/evals/**`

## Before editing

1. Check overlapping AGENTS / rules / skills; prefer a reference over a copy.
2. Keep universal rules short; keep specialist rules scoped (`alwaysApply: false`).
3. Preserve positive and negative skill-routing boundaries in skill frontmatter
   and routing evals.
4. After material instruction or routing changes, run:

```bash
python3 tools/agent-config/validate-agent-instruction-hygiene.py
python3 tools/agent-config/validate-agent-instruction-hygiene.py --self-test
bash tools/skills/validate-all-skills.sh
```

## Forbid

- Broad `**/*` specialist rules without demonstrated need
- Duplicate active skills
- Copying generic framework guidance without reconciling Debina versions
- Secret-read / credential-exfiltration instructions
- Credential material combined with outbound network commands
- Remote pipe-to-shell or decoded remote bootstrap
- Persistent Git/package/shell/system hooks
- TLS / security-control bypass instructions
- Unsafe credential-bearing config dumps
- Invisible or bidirectional Unicode control characters
- Non-template environment files used as instruction inputs (allow `.env.example` / `.env.sample` / `.env.template` only)

Do not make this rule `alwaysApply: true`.
